= Internet — Simple =

The Internet is a global system of interconnected computer networks that communicate using the Internet protocol suite.

It links independently operated networks through common addressing, routing, transport, and application-layer conventions. The Internet is infrastructure for many services, including the Web, email, messaging, streaming, and remote computation.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* Internet ≠ World Wide Web
* Internet ≠ one network operator

